// FlowSeer SNMP integration T2 — SR Linux startup configuration.
//
// Provisions:
//   - SNMPv2c community "public" (read-only) for sanity probes.
//   - SNMPv3 USM user "flowseer" with SHA-256 auth + AES-256 priv.
//     Credentials match testenv.SRLinuxUSMConfig so the readiness
//     probe and downstream tests agree on the user state.
//
// The passphrase literals below are non-secret integration-test
// values pinned for deterministic test runs against the ephemeral
// containerlab-managed SR Linux node; do NOT copy them into
// production USM configurations.
//
// Loaded by the containerlab topology's `startup-config` field at
// boot. The exact SR Linux CLI syntax for SNMP has evolved across
// 23.x → 24.x; commands below target the 24.x release line. If the
// containerlab pull resolves to a release where these commands are
// rejected (visible as a deploy error in
// `containerlab deploy -t srlinux.clab.yaml`), the iteration target
// is THIS file — the Go harness assumes only that some valid CLI
// provisions the documented USM user.

enter candidate

/ system snmp community public {
    type ro-only
}

/ system snmp engine-id local-engine-id 80004f0103aabbccdd

/ system snmp v3 user flowseer {
    authentication {
        protocol sha2-256
        password "flowseer-auth-passphrase"
    }
    privacy {
        protocol aes-256-cfb
        password "flowseer-priv-passphrase"
    }
}

/ system snmp network-instance mgmt {
    admin-state enable
    udp-server [
        {
            ip-address ::
            port 161
        }
    ]
}

commit save
